{"nodes": [{"id": "src_dev_mount_loop_teardown_harness", "label": "Mount/Unmount Teardown Harness (mount-loop.html)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/dev/mount-loop.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Browsers cap live WebGL contexts at around 16, so twenty iterations that all reach a first frame is itself the leak test; each iteration reports whether the previous context was released and whether the subtree was removed. Run by hand before any change to teardown-sensitive code merges - it is the only teardown check, as there is no automated one."}, {"id": "src_dev_mount_loop_metateardown", "label": "metaTeardown", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/dev/mount-loop.html", "source_location": "lines 314-338", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "meta.json content is read with an await before the asset is registered, so a destroy can land inside it and the continuation must not touch the app it just lost; driven with a contents promise the page controls so the timing is exact rather than a race with the network."}], "edges": [{"source": "src_dev_mount_loop_teardown_harness", "target": "docs_api_createviewer", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/dev/mount-loop.html", "source_location": "lines 326, 357, 1212", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_dev_mount_loop_teardown_harness", "target": "docs_api_destroy", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/dev/mount-loop.html", "source_location": "lines 333, 486, 965, 1247", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_dev_mount_loop_teardown_harness", "target": "docs_api_captureframe", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/dev/mount-loop.html", "source_location": "lines 865, 1161, 1220", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_dev_mount_l